{
  "description": "Type the failure for a VMID that names no container on the node. Calls under /nodes/{node}/lxc/{vmid} load the guest's configuration, and PVE::AbstractConfig::load_config dies with \"Configuration file 'nodes/<node>/lxc/<vmid>.conf' does not exist\\n\", which the API server answers as HTTP 500 with that message in the JSON body (PVE::APIServer::Formatter::Standard). As a 500 it would surface as a retryable InternalServerError; it is a not-found. Sources: https://git.proxmox.com/?p=pve-guest-common.git;a=blob;f=src/PVE/AbstractConfig.pm (load_config), https://git.proxmox.com/?p=pve-http-server.git;a=blob;f=src/PVE/APIServer/Formatter/Standard.pm (prepare_response_data).",
  "patches": [
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/shapes/proxmox.nodes_lxc#GuestNotFound",
      "value": {
        "type": "structure",
        "members": {
          "code": {
            "target": "smithy.api#Integer"
          },
          "message": {
            "target": "smithy.api#String"
          }
        },
        "traits": {
          "smithy.api#error": "client",
          "smithy.api#httpError": 404,
          "smithy.api#documentation": "The VMID names no container on this node: Proxmox answers HTTP 500 \"Configuration file 'nodes/<node>/lxc/<vmid>.conf' does not exist\".",
          "com.distilled.openapi#errorMatchers": [
            {
              "status": 500,
              "message": {
                "matches": "^Configuration file 'nodes/[^/']+/lxc/[0-9]+\\.conf' does not exist$"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
